  m_text: 'A faked beam is a cone mesh with a transparent, additive material. It is drawn like any other object: it receives no light and knows nothing of shadows.


    <b>Predict:</b> Lamp A has a Spot Light in the volumetric fog; lamp B has a cone. You move the Panel under each lamp. What happens to each beam?


    <b>Try:</b> Move the Panel under lamp A, then under lamp B. Keep whichever beam the picture needs. (In the Volumetric Fog override, Enable Additional Lights Contribution must be ticked.)


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 10, 11</color></size>'
