  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Volumetric fog gives the air a density. Along each view ray the air dims what lies behind it and adds the light that reaches it. Where a wall casts a shadow into the air, no light is added.


    <b>Predict:</b> The Sun low behind the slit, volumetric fog on: where will the light show in the air? Is the fog brighter looking toward the Sun, or away from it?


    <b>Try:</b> Set the Sun''s Intensity to 2 and its Rotation to X 12, Y 0. Select the Volume, Add Override > Custom > Volumetric Fog, tick Enabled and Enable Main Light Contribution. Then set the ambient to black: what happens to the fog in shadow?


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 12, 17</color></size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
